  "sourceProvenance": "Sources identify the compiled full-catalog run. Subsequent MagPonderPlugin changes adjust camera, caption or hint layout in Fusion Panel, Railgun Pair, rare-earth magnets and Copycats; their focused reruns are in the combined report. All thermal/power builders, assertions, text, targets and schematic match the tested files.",
  "english": {
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.header": "Activate Pyrrhotite with heat",
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.text_1": "Cold Pyrrhotite emits no field. Blue cells illustrate field strength; heat must touch the block or a catalyst that can reach it.",
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.text_2": "A smouldering or fading Blaze Burner gives WEAK strength. A lit campfire also gives WEAK.",
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.text_3": "A kindled Blaze Burner gives STRONG strength. Fire and Magma Blocks give the same tier.",
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.text_4": "A seething Blaze Burner gives EXTREME strength. Lava also gives EXTREME; heat levels do not add together.",
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.text_5": "The basic catalyst relays its adjacent heat to Pyrrhotite up to 3 blocks away. The blue line shows this reach.",
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.text_6": "An Enhanced Catalyst reaches 5 blocks. The heat source must still touch the catalyst.",
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.text_7": "A Cosmic Catalyst reaches 7 blocks. Range is measured independently along each axis, not along a cable.",
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.text_8": "Catalysts cannot chain. This heated basic catalyst is 6 blocks away; the unheated middle catalyst cannot extend its range.",
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.text_9": "The hottest source in range wins. Here the Enhanced Catalyst supplies EXTREME despite the weaker basic source.",
    "magnetization.ponder.pyrrhotite_heat.text_10": "Remove the heat sources and the field ends on the next heat scan. The server controls active and idle scan intervals.",
    "magnetization.ponder.gyrostabilizer.header": "Stop ship rotation, keep translation",
    "magnetization.ponder.gyrostabilizer.text_1": "Mount the Gyrostabilizer aboard a ship. This moving section illustrates a ship translating and rotating while unpowered.",
    "magnetization.ponder.gyrostabilizer.text_2": "Power it with adjacent redstone. It cancels angular velocity while translation continues; it does not anchor the ship in place.",
    "magnetization.ponder.gyrostabilizer.text_3": "FE is an alternative: stabilization costs 20 FE per tick. Gold marks an external FE supply. Redstone power takes priority and uses no FE.",
    "magnetization.ponder.gyrostabilizer.text_4": "Remove both power sources and rotation is free again. A powered Gyrostabilizer on the ground has no ship to stabilize and spends no FE.",
    "magnetization.ponder.induction_pad.header": "Charge carried FE equipment",
    "magnetization.ponder.induction_pad.text_1": "Induction Pads require the server to enable inductionPadEnabled; it is off by default. This tutorial shows the enabled behavior.",
    "magnetization.ponder.induction_pad.text_2": "Supply FE through a cable or generator. Gold marks the external supply; the pad stores energy for nearby equipment.",
    "magnetization.ponder.induction_pad.text_3": "The gold token represents carried equipment that accepts FE. Green cells illustrate its charge increasing as the pad spends energy; ordinary tools do not charge.",
    "magnetization.ponder.induction_pad.text_4": "Charging checks inventory, offhand and worn armor, plus enabled Curios slots. Stand within the configured area: by default 4 blocks beyond each pad face.",
    "magnetization.ponder.induction_pad.text_5": "Leaving that area stops charging. An empty pad also cannot charge; transfer rate, scan interval and range are server configurable."
  },
